# Tier 3 of the merge tiers (DamDamDio/admin-platform#169): security and rules, which only the owner approves and
# merges. With the organization ruleset `owner-paths` ("Require review from Code Owners"), GitHub refuses to merge a
# pull request that changes a file listed here until @drossello approves its latest diff.
#
# This repository is public, and GitHub serves its default files to every repository of the organization that has no
# file of that type of its own. So every file is the owner's, a new one included (a SECURITY.md, a pull request
# template, or profile/README.md, which shows on the organization's public page).
#
# The issue forms too, although #169 puts the backlog's vocabulary in tier 2: a merge here publishes them, which the
# proxies may not decide ("making anything public" is one of their hard limits), and in this repository no machine
# check reads the proxies' approval. To make the forms tier 2, add a last line `/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/` with no
# owner: the last matching line wins, and a line with no owner leaves its files without a code owner.
* @drossello

# This file, by name and last, so that no later line can take its owner away.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @drossello
